Topi Ylinen (f1toyl@uta.fi) wrote:
: Several months ago, there was a thread like this one in rec.games.frp.dnd,
: and people posted what they thought was inspiring music for characters of
: different classes. I just wonder if we could find music for Nethack characters
[snip]


: 	Caveman: Dunno, maybe Stravinsky's Rite...

There's already a perfect theme for this, and it runs thru MY head whenever
I hit 'C' after the "What type of character do you want to be?" prompt:

The theme to the movie _Caveman_ of course! Music by Lalo Schifrin, movie
starred Ringo Starr and Shelley Long. Very cute theme. Very cro-magnon-ish :-)


: 	Elf, Healer: No idea.

In Shadowrun novels, and in many of the Terry Brooks and Tolkien books, Elves
are given very Celtic / Gaelic names and legends. So probably the music that
would best fit this theme would be Enya. In particular, "Cursum Perficio" from
_Watermark_ and _March of the Celts_ from her first CD might fit for a warlike
or peaceful character, respectively.


: 	Priest: Anything by Tallis or Allegri.

Or if you want to be more modern about it, Enigma. No wait, dont laugh! They
use Gregorian chants -- the "typical Latin priest music" of the Middle Ages!

: 	Rogue: No idea here, either. 

Army marching songs? :-)

: 	Samurai: Anyone know a good soundtrack from a Japanese movie? Something
: 	by Toru Takemitsu, perhaps?

The theme to _Ran_ (Akira Kurosawa's last film) is pretty ominous.
And for some reason, I've always associated Vangelis' music with things
Japanese.

: 	Tourist: Hmmm... almost anything goes here :-) Next time I play tourist
: 	on my home computer, I think I'll listen to Glenn Miller...

What if he's a student tourist? Erik B and Rakim!! :-D

: 	Valkyrie: Need I say it? "The Ride of the Valkyries", of course. Only
: 	too bad you cannot rename Odin to Wotan (the Germanic form, as in 
: 	Wagner's operas). 

Okay, but kinda common. Do also check out Donner's storm calling-song, in
Wagner's _Das Rheingold_. I think it's near the end of Act 1. PERFECT if you
have Mjollnir, cuz at the climax when Donner hurls his hammer (guess what
it's called?) the orchestra percussion section actually hits an anvil followed
by tympani rolls... eerily like lightning and thunder...

: 	Wizard: The last movement from Holst's "Planets". Maybe.

Good choice!! Maybe if you're feeling corny, you could include "The Sorcerors
Apprentice", but it would kinda give me the image of my wizard looking like
Mickey Mouse :-)p

: Well, any other ideas?

Well, your last one makes me think of the "Mars" movement from _The Planets_.
What could that be used for? Technically, Mars corresponds to Odin, so...

